From 23df986bd30a30c30e9456c07e32ec533f20ebea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:24:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: fix patch-0004 binding clobber (manifest actions dead
 on arrival)

Patch 0004 made load_action_manifest suggest the manifest bindings for a profile
(e.g. oculus/touch_controller), then unconditionally call the legacy path whose
closure re-suggested legacy bindings for EVERY profile -- including the one just
bound. xrSuggestInteractionProfileBindings REPLACES (not merges) per profile, so
the legacy call wiped the manifest bindings before the single attach_action_sets.
Every manifest action ended up with zero bound sources -> is_active=false forever
(live capture on Aircar: 0 of 123010 true, session FOCUSED, controllers connected,
profile bound).

Fix: a profile the manifest binds now gets ONE suggest carrying the union of
manifest + legacy bindings (load_bindings_for_profile folds in
legacy_bindings_for_profile); suggest_legacy_bindings_except handles the remaining
profiles the manifest did not cover. Splits get_or_create_legacy_actions into
get_or_create_legacy_action_data (create only) + the two suggest helpers.

Live A/B confirmed on Aircar (1073390), real G2 hardware: is_active 0 -> 224928
true, current_state=true on real presses; wearer confirmed Y=music, A=start,
flight all work. Explains why patch 0011 (sync-race fix) never helped -- this
clobber happens earlier, at bind/attach time. Known-benign follow-up: pose_data.grip
is bound twice in the merged call (Monado tolerates duplicate binding pairs; proven
harmless live) -- dedup later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016hLhNFWNfr9kz98qXtoftw
